bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    struct_two_traits_same_method_resolve_silently_native_2026-11-26, 0, "Two traits that both declare mark, both implemented for one struct in the same module (trait Marker and trait Other, impl Marker for P returns 1000 + v, impl Other for P returns 2000 + v), and a call p.mark() with both traits in scope: the aarch64 Stage 2 at 76892f19a3a native-builds it on llvm (rc=0) and prints m=2001, silently picking Other.mark. The same shape on a primitive Self (impl Marker for i32 and impl Other for i32) is rejected with ambiguous scalar trait method: mark. The struct call is just as ambiguous and should be rejected or require trait selection, not resolved by declaration order. Found by the two_struct probe in the 2026-11-26 aarch64 verification lane (primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07)."

